# This directory is intentionally empty for now.
#
# It must exist: `Package.swift` declares a `JanelaSessionTests` target, and
# SwiftPM warns about a target whose sources directory is missing.
#
# What belongs here once `JanelaSession` does something (docs/testing.md):
#
#   - All five `SessionCreationRequest` cases, using an in-memory database and a
#     fake `WorktreeServing`. The point is the orchestration, not git.
#   - The product rule that worktree creation is one case of `createSession`,
#     not a separate entry point — assert there is no second public creator.
#   - The invariants tying `backing` to `projectID`: a `.folder` session has no
#     project, a `.projectDirectory` session must have one, and neither may ever
#     report `ownsItsDirectory`.
#   - `removeSession`: that it never deletes a directory unless the plan says so
#     *and* the caller opted in, and that a `.sessionTeardown` command which never
#     exits is abandoned at its timeout rather than hanging deletion.
#   - Automation ordering: `.worktreeCreated` runs after the include copy and
#     before `.sessionStart`, and a non-zero exit leaves the session usable.
#   - Attention policy against a recording `AttentionDelivering`: no delivery for
#     the focused terminal, none while the app is frontmost, and four bells in five
#     seconds produce one delivery (docs/decisions/0011-notifications.md).
#   - `ProjectStore.setExpanded` does no I/O. If expanding a project ever needs a
#     fake for git or the filesystem, the laziness rule has been broken.
